        },
        {
          "code": "A1",
          "desc": "Differentiating each term correctly"
        }
      ],
      "solution": "$\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(\\ln(x\\sqrt{x^2+4})\\right) = \\frac{d}{dx}\\left(\\ln x + \\ln(x^2+4)^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\right)$\n$= \\frac{d}{dx}\\left(\\ln x + \\frac{1}{2}\\ln(x^2+4)\\right)$\n$= \\frac{1}{x} + \\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\frac{2x}{x^2+4}\\right)$\n$= \\frac{1}{x} + \\frac{x}{x^2+4}$",
      "ai_explanation": {
