      "solution": "$\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(\\ln\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{x^2+1}}{(x+3)(x-2)}\\right)\\right) = \\frac{d}{dx}\\left(\\ln(x^2+1)^{\\frac{1}{2}} - \\ln((x+3)(x-2))\\right)$\n$= \\frac{d}{dx}\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\ln(x^2+1) - \\ln(x+3) - \\ln(x-2)\\right)$\n$= \\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\frac{2x}{x^2+1}\\right) - \\frac{1}{x+3} - \\frac{1}{x-2}$\n$= \\frac{x}{x^2+1} - \\frac{1}{x+3} - \\frac{1}{x-2}$",
